### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Cross-channel memory demo — click "Send Request" above each block
### (needs the REST Client extension; start a demo console config first)
### Customer Maya Patel = CUST-1001, Daniel Okafor = CUST-1002
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 0 · Health check — shows backend (vertex/local) and model
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### What does memory know about Maya before we start?
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/CUST-1001/memories?q=travel

### 1 · WEB CHAT (identified by Account ID) — Maya shares a trip
POST {{baseUrl}}/channels/web-chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "account_id": "ACC-77310042",
  "message": "I'm flying to Lisbon on November 10, please remember that. Will my card work there?"
}

### 2 · VOICE (identified by caller number) — she never mentions Lisbon
POST {{baseUrl}}/channels/voice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "caller_number": "+1 (212) 555-0142",
  "transcript": "Hi, I'm calling about my trip."
}

### 3 · EMAIL (identified by sender address) — formal style, cites the dispute
POST {{baseUrl}}/channels/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sender": "Maya Patel <maya.patel@example.com>",
  "subject": "Hotel charge",
  "body": "Any update on the hotel charge?"
}

### 4 · EMAIL — a new contact preference
POST {{baseUrl}}/channels/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sender": "maya.patel@example.com",
  "subject": "Calls",
  "body": "Only call me after 6pm from now on."
}

### 5 · NEW CHAT SESSION — recall from long-term memory
POST {{baseUrl}}/channels/web-chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "account_id": "ACC-77310042",
  "message": "What have I told you about travel and when to call me?"
}

### Memory after the conversation
GET {{baseUrl}}/customers/CUST-1001/memories?q=travel%20call%20preference

### 6 · ISOLATION — Daniel calls; nothing of Maya's should appear
POST {{baseUrl}}/channels/voice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "caller_number": "+1 (646) 555-0177",
  "transcript": "Where's my replacement card?"
}

### 7 · OPTIONAL — all three channels at once, one memory
POST {{baseUrl}}/demo/concurrent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "web_chat": { "account_id": "ACC-77310042", "message": "Is my Lisbon trip noted?" },
  "voice":    { "caller_number": "+12125550142", "transcript": "When will you call me back?" },
  "email":    { "sender": "maya.patel@example.com", "body": "Please confirm my travel notice." }
}
